# chat — a minimal, self-contained chat pipeline: a basic AI assistant.
#
#   evoke chat chat
#
# Evoke starts a llama.cpp backend for the session and shuts it down on exit.
# `model` names a GGUF file (like an IMAGE checkpoint); Evoke finds it in the
# directories set under chat.model_paths in ~/.evoke/settings.json, so this file
# stays portable — it names the model, not a machine path. The free-text lines
# are the system prompt.

TAGS
    chat
    assistant

CHAT
    backend = llama.cpp
    model = qwen2.5.gguf

    context_window = 8192
    gpu_layers = 99
    max_output_tokens = 512
    temperature = 0.7

    You are a helpful, harmless, and honest AI assistant.
    Answer clearly and concisely. If you are unsure or do not know something, say so instead of making it up.
